{"id": "EUVD-2026-93208", "enisaUuid": "57427bb9-4709-3710-80d3-d46d626a6b59", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/xe/i2c: Disable IRQ on unbind\n\nCurrently, struct xe_i2c is freed before SGUnit IRQ is disabled in unbind\npath, leaving a potential UAF in case I2C IRQ is hit during this small\nwindow. Explicitly disable I2C IRQ in xe_i2c_remove() and fix this.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 8ba5c8b8ab3fd362267c11df2cd5a90ee46f6e24)", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/571ccbc801aa4d22a22d9f924b826c77052330f0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0e9f963a3d209d7dc7ddd61116118ab5da2797d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98280", "GHSA-jc76-pp47-fx9m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a626634-28da-30f6-8a9f-163186d7d788", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1355f13c-a0a8-3494-b8b7-806479345bde", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}, {"id": "57f81a32-277e-32cc-a0d9-07e321ac9df5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0bb78ce099265fba3808c05de1c75c649664a6cb <571ccbc801aa4d22a22d9f924b826c77052330f0"}, {"id": "90469388-d63f-3d36-889d-fb3f0f5774a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "96499dfd-5d10-3dad-95df-ddc9dd61288b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0bb78ce099265fba3808c05de1c75c649664a6cb <f0e9f963a3d209d7dc7ddd61116118ab5da2797d"}, {"id": "ebe5e25e-3a75-38e0-9552-e324250b8ad7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6af7b623-b772-3f21-af89-f199b21d4d41", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}